{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107316-a-few-questions","id":1107316,"title":"A few questions.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-24T08:08:10-07:00","id":1107316,"title":"A few questions.","content":"In M20 corebook at page 545 it says as follows: All-out Reality-fucking, however, is hard to endure. Vulgar attacks of pure reality-alteration power (curses, transmutations, possession, etc.) cannot be soaked unless the target has countermagick or some other specific protection against the Effect in question.<br /> Wouldn't it mean that attacks such as forces' flames etcetera (Since its legit transmutation of elements) would be unsoakable by anyone who doesnt have countermagick dice pool?<br /> AKA nightfolk such garou and vamps etc. Since their innate countermagic doesnt really apply if they just burst out into flames (innate nightfolk countermagic is wits + occult diff 7 if im not mistaken), because afaik the innate Countermagic pool applies only if the patterns are directly under magical effects.<br /> So they cant soak it at all?<br /> <br /> Another question I've got, regarding life 3. Say I grow gills or scales over my skin to get armor/more dicepool for soaking. How would that work, do I follow Effect &amp; Duration chart? aka if i get 8 successes in a ritual, i spend 3 for duration (which means a day), leaving me with 5 for the effect. So I'll have 5 additional soaking dicepool for a whole day? Is that how it works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T09:25:28-07:00","id":1107336,"title":"","content":"Crossover rule of thumb: There is no generally accepted mandate, just do whatever makes sense and tweak it if it breaks.<br /> <br /> Personally, I interpret &quot;vulgar attacks of pure reality-alteration power&quot; to be direct pattern damage alla Rip the Man Body, Entropy cursing, or turning someone's flesh into stone. Unless you're attacking an elemental, the magic in a Forces effect just creates or moulds the energy before you, and then you fling that at them. Fire can be soaked if you have fire proof stuff on (magic or otherwise), as can electric stuff if you have some kind of grounding device to hand. Otherwise it's aggravated.<br /> <br /> Regarding the splitting of successes, that's a good way to do it. I mean, that's pretty much how I enforce magic rolls on my games anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}